---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { atlas } from '../lib/data'

const counts = {
  models: Object.keys(atlas.models).length,
  providers: Object.keys(atlas.providers).length,
  offerings: Object.values(atlas.providers).reduce((n, p) => n + Object.keys(p.models).length, 0)
}
---

<Base title="About & API">
  <h1>About model-atlas</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    An open, source-annotated database of LLM and text-to-image models — {counts.models} open-weights models,
    {counts.offerings} API offerings across {counts.providers} providers.
  </p>

  <h2>Why another model database?</h2>
  <p>
    models.dev covers LLM API pricing well and LiteLLM ships a pricing JSON, but three things were missing everywhere:
    unified <strong>text-to-image coverage</strong> (open-weights specs joined with API pricing normalized to $/image),
    <strong>hardware fit as data</strong> (measured VRAM and throughput per model × quant × GPU), and
    <strong>Korean benchmark scores</strong> (KMMLU, LogicKor) in machine-readable form. This project fills those gaps
    and credits its upstreams.
  </p>

  <h2>Use the data</h2>
  <p>Everything on this site is one JSON file, CC-BY-4.0:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th><code>/api.json</code></th><td>Full dataset: models, providers, offerings, benchmarks, hardware</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Every numeric fact carries <code>source.url</code> and <code>source.as_of</code>. The dataset is maintained in TOML
    (one file per model) on GitHub, refreshed by a daily deterministic sync plus a Claude-based curator agent whose
    changes land as reviewable pull requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Contributing</h2>
  <p>
    Add or fix a model with a PR — schema validation runs in CI. Measured VRAM / tok/s / sec-per-image data points from
    your own hardware are especially welcome.
  </p>
</Base>
